>I counted something on the order of about 300 segments.  I applied
>a stethoscope to the worm's body and learned it had 500 HP.  *woof*
>
>I'm assuming that the worm's size is a result of both the available
>space (because I dug out all the walls) and because it had lots of
>time to grow while I was busy elsewhere.  I don't know if this is a
>record, but it's got to be close.  I've never seen anything quite
>like it.

A long worm grows fairly quickly with time.  About every 10 turns 
(on average) it will increase its length by 1.  If your long worm
had about 300 segments, that means you spent about 3000 turns on that
level since the worm was created.  Sound about right?
